Palette and community-port exception

Notwithstanding the paragraph above, the copyright holder grants permission
to use, copy, modify, and redistribute the machine-readable color data,
loaders, schemas, and generated community-port fixtures distributed inside
`@auralis-labs/palettes`, `packages/auralis-palettes`, `ports/palettes.json`,
and `ports/community-fixtures` for either of these purposes:

1. rendering Auralis colors in syntax highlighters or documentation; or
2. building and distributing an Auralis port for another application.

This exception does not cover Auralis SVG/file/product icon artwork, extension
runtime code, Marketplace media, or other assets. A redistributed port must
retain this notice, identify material color changes, link to
https://syntalume.dev, and must not claim to be an official first-party
release. A port may be bundled with a free or paid-adjacent product but may not
be sold as a standalone palette or theme. "Auralis" may be used only to
identify compatibility or the source palette; no other trademark or brand
rights are granted. All other rights remain reserved.

Third-party notice

The Auralis Product Icons font is generated from original Auralis glyph SVGs. No
Microsoft Codicons font, glyph artwork, or font binaries are bundled in or
shipped with this extension.

The `@vscode/codicons` package is used only as a build-time development
dependency. Its metadata mapping (icon identifiers, categories, and tags)
informs the coverage of Auralis product icon ids; no Codicons glyph artwork is
copied or shipped. `@vscode/codicons` is published by Microsoft under the
Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International (CC-BY-4.0) license. See
https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/ for the license text.

